# Line endings are pinned to LF.
#
# native/build.sh gates on `gofmt -l`, and gofmt reports every CRLF file as unformatted.
# With `eol` unspecified, a Windows checkout converts text to CRLF (core.autocrlf is true
# on GitHub's Windows runners), so the native build failed there on a check that passes on
# Linux and macOS — all twelve .go files were reported at once, which is the signature of a
# line-ending problem rather than twelve formatting mistakes. Found by the three-OS CI gate.
*.go   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.qk   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf

# Committed build outputs are binary and must never be line-ending converted.
*.so   binary
*.dll  binary
native/clegnative binary
